ROS 2 message definitions (.msg files), for the schemas of recorded topics.

An MCAP file of ROS 2 topics carries each topic's definition and the
definitions it uses (schema encoding "ros2msg", as rosbag2 writes it), so
that ros2 bag and other readers (Foxglove) can decode the messages without
the console. These are the .msg files of the ROS 2 Jazzy packages
std_msgs, builtin_interfaces, geometry_msgs, sensor_msgs, rcl_interfaces,
nav_msgs, diagnostic_msgs, visualization_msgs, example_interfaces and
service_msgs, copied unchanged from a Jazzy install (/opt/ros/jazzy/share/
<package>/msg/*.msg; https://github.com/ros2/common_interfaces,
https://github.com/ros2/rcl_interfaces, https://github.com/ros2/example_interfaces).
They are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt), as their packages declare (package.xml).
Copyright in the definitions belongs to their authors (Open Source Robotics
Foundation, Inc. and the ROS 2 contributors).

Types of other packages are looked up in the share directories of a ROS 2
install named by AMENT_PREFIX_PATH, when there is one; else their schema is
written empty (encoding "unknown"), as rosbag2 does when it cannot find a
definition.

Refresh with (in a ROS 2 Jazzy container):

  cd /opt/ros/jazzy/share && tar cf - <package>/msg/*.msg | tar xf - -C vendor/msgdefs
